    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0811" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg799"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/10–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Embassy to the
                            Department of State
                    </hi><anchor n="92" xml:id="d770-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1945-10-27">October 27, 1945</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Text of a Telegram From the Foreign Office Dated
                        October</hi> 27<hi rendition="#small-caps">th</hi>, 1945</p>
                <p>I do not want to risk failure to agree with the United States Government on the
                    terms of reference when we are so close.</p>
                <p>Byrnes has told you that if the United States Government were to agree to
                    transposition of (1) and (2) of the terms of reference, they would find it
                    extremely difficult to consent to the retention of the words “or other countries
                    outside Europe” in our re-draft of the original No. 2 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >3?</hi>].</p>
                <pb facs="0812" n="800" xml:id="pg800"/>
                <p>You have authority to revert to the original order of terms of reference provided
                    that we can keep the words “or other countries outside Europe”, to which I
                    attach very great importance.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d770-f1" n="92" type="source" xml:id="d770-f1-content">
                <p>Forwarded to the Deputy Director of the Office of Near Eastern Affairs (Allen) by
                    the British Minister (Balfour) on October 27, 1945.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
